IMPORT prelude

-- Consumer Protection (Trade Descriptions and Safety Requirements) Act 1975 (Singapore) -- what a trade description is and when
-- one is false (ss 2, 5), the false trade description offence (s 4), the Schedule carve-out (ss 2(2), 13), the civil action for
-- breach of safety regulations (s 11(3)), false claims of official supply or approval (s 14), penalties, time bar, directors and
-- defences (ss 15 to 17, 19 to 21, 24), forfeiture of seized goods (s 26(3)) and compensation orders (s 31).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation ("version in force from 1/7/2025"), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/CPTDSRA1975.txt. The latest amendment annotated in the body is Act 13 of 2025 (wef 1 July 2025: the
-- "Safety Authority" definition in s 2 and s 32); the Schedule is annotated S 796/2023 (wef 8 December 2023).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Chosen for its everyday-life relevance to ordinary people in Singapore: it is the law behind a label, an expiry date,
-- a "genuine leather" tag, a gold-fineness stamp or a claim that a product is "government approved", and behind the safety rules for
-- consumer goods. (An automated count found none of the 527 deposited Singapore Acts citing it by this title; that count undercounts
-- older and short titles and is not a measure of importance.) The Act is short, so most of it is encoded. Not encoded: s 3
-- (appointments), s 6 (what "applying" a description means -- taken as a single input), s 7 (advertisements referring to a class of
-- goods), s 8 (pre-1975 trade marks), ss 9, 10, 12 (informative marking and advertisement regulations, whose content lives in
-- subsidiary legislation not retrieved), s 18 (liability of the person at fault), ss 22, 23, 25, 27, 28, 30 (enforcement powers and
-- procedure), s 32 (regulations). s 29 (contracts not void) is noted, not modelled.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Consumer Protection (Trade Descriptions and Safety Requirements) Act 1975 -- descriptions`

§§ `2(1) -- what a trade description is about`

-- s 2(1): "trade description" means any description, statement or indication which, "directly or indirectly and by whatever means
-- given", relates to: (a) quantity, length, width, height, area, volume, capacity or weight; (b) method of manufacture, production,
-- processing or reconditioning; (c) composition; (d) "fitness for purpose (including expiry date), strength, performance, behaviour
-- or accuracy"; (e) degree of fineness of gold and silver goods; (f) other physical characteristics; (g) testing and its results;
-- (h) approval by any person or conformity with an approved type; (i) place or date of manufacture; (j) the maker; (k) "other
-- history, including previous ownership or use".
-- The list does not mention PRICE, nor the seller's own terms (refunds, warranties as a contract term). The last two values below
-- are such matters; that they fall outside the list is a reading of the list, not a statement in the text.
DECLARE Matter IS ONE OF
    `quantity or weight`
    `method of manufacture`
    `composition`
    `fitness for purpose or expiry date`
    `fineness of gold or silver`
    `testing and its results`
    `approval by any person`
    `place or date of manufacture`
    `who made the goods`
    `previous ownership or use`
    `the price`
    `the seller's refund policy`

GIVEN `the matter` IS A Matter
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a trade description matter` IF
    CONSIDER `the matter`
    WHEN `the price` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the seller's refund policy` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `4, 5, 2(2), 2(4) -- the false trade description offence`

-- s 4: "any person who in the course of a trade or business -- (a) applies a false trade description to any goods; or (b) supplies
-- any goods to which a false trade description is applied, shall be guilty of an offence."
-- s 5(a)(i): a false trade description is one which "by reason of anything contained in or omitted from" it "is false or likely to
-- mislead in a material respect".
-- s 2(2): where a trade description is subject to a law in the Schedule (Sale of Food Act 1973, Health Products Act 2007, Electric
-- Vehicles Charging Act 2022), the Act does not have effect for a description "applied in accordance with the requirements of that
-- written law".
-- s 2(4): a trade description published in a newspaper, book, periodical, film or broadcast is not "applied in the course of a trade
-- or business unless it is or forms part of an advertisement".
DECLARE Dealing HAS
    `is in the course of a trade or business` IS A BOOLEAN
    `applies the description or supplies goods bearing it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the matter described` IS A Matter
    `is false or likely to mislead` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in a material respect` IS A BOOLEAN
    `appears only in a newspaper, book, periodical, film or broadcast` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is or forms part of an advertisement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is applied in accordance with a Schedule law` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the dealing` IS A Dealing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a false trade description` IF
        `is a trade description matter` (`the dealing`'s `the matter described`)
    AND `the dealing`'s `is false or likely to mislead`
    AND `the dealing`'s `in a material respect`

GIVEN `the dealing` IS A Dealing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `counts as in the course of a trade or business` IF
        `the dealing`'s `is in the course of a trade or business`
    AND (    (NOT `the dealing`'s `appears only in a newspaper, book, periodical, film or broadcast`)
         OR  `the dealing`'s `is or forms part of an advertisement`)

GIVEN `the dealing` IS A Dealing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commits the section 4 offence` IF
        `counts as in the course of a trade or business` `the dealing`
    AND `the dealing`'s `applies the description or supplies goods bearing it`
    AND `is a false trade description` `the dealing`
    AND (NOT `the dealing`'s `is applied in accordance with a Schedule law`)

§§ `11(3), 13 -- suing over unsafe goods`

-- s 11(2): supplying, in the course of a trade or business, goods in contravention of safety regulations made under s 11 is an
-- offence. s 11(3): the contravention "is deemed to be a breach of a statutory duty for which action may be brought by any other
-- person who may be affected by the contravention".
-- s 13: "The provisions of this Part [Part 3, ss 9 to 13] do not apply to any goods which are subject to and regulated by" a Schedule
-- law. Unlike s 2(2), this carve-out does not ask whether the Schedule law was complied with.
GIVEN `supplied in the course of a trade or business` IS A BOOLEAN, `contravened safety regulations under s 11` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the claimant was affected` IS A BOOLEAN, `the goods are regulated by a Schedule law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may sue for breach of statutory duty` IF
        `supplied in the course of a trade or business`
    AND `contravened safety regulations under s 11`
    AND `the claimant was affected`
    AND (NOT `the goods are regulated by a Schedule law`)

§§ `14 -- false claims of official supply or approval`

-- s 14(1): any person who in the course of a trade or business "gives by whatever means any false indication, direct or indirect,
-- that any goods supplied by the person or any methods adopted by the person are or are of a kind supplied to or approved by any
-- person including any government or government department or agency or any international body" commits an offence.
GIVEN `acts in the course of a trade or business` IS A BOOLEAN, `indicates supply to or approval by someone` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the indication is true` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commits the section 14 offence` IF
        `acts in the course of a trade or business`
    AND `indicates supply to or approval by someone`
    AND (NOT `the indication is true`)

§§ `15, 24 -- maximum penalties`

-- s 15: an offence "for which no other penalty is specified" -- a fine not exceeding $10,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 2 years
-- or both. s 24(1): obstructing an officer, or failing to comply with a s 23 requirement or to give assistance -- $2,000 or one year
-- or both; s 24(2): knowingly false statement in such information -- the same. s 23(4) (disclosing trade secrets or information
-- obtained under the Act) states no penalty, so s 15 applies to it.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `applying or supplying a false trade description`
    `false claim of official approval`
    `unlawful disclosure of information`
    `obstructing an officer`
    `false statement to an officer`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `obstructing an officer` THEN 2000
    WHEN `false statement to an officer` THEN 2000
    OTHERWISE 10000

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `obstructing an officer` THEN 12
    WHEN `false statement to an officer` THEN 12
    OTHERWISE 24

§§ `16, 21 -- time bar and composition`

-- s 16: "No prosecution ... may be commenced after the expiry of 3 years from the commission of the offence." Time is in months
-- here; a prosecution at exactly 36 months is taken as not yet "after the expiry".
-- s 21: the Director may compound any offence "by accepting ... a sum not exceeding $2,000".
GIVEN `months since the offence` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a prosecution may still be commenced` IF
    `months since the offence` AT MOST 36

GIVEN `the sum offered` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the sum is within the composition limit` IF
    `the sum offered` AT MOST 2000

§§ `17 -- officers of companies`

-- s 17: where an offence by a body corporate "is proved to have been committed with the consent and connivance of, or to be
-- attributable to any neglect on the part of, any director, manager, secretary or other similar officer", that person "as well as
-- the body corporate shall be guilty". The text says "consent AND connivance", conjunctively; it is encoded as written.
GIVEN `the company committed an offence` IS A BOOLEAN, `the officer consented` IS A BOOLEAN, `the officer connived` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `it is attributable to the officer's neglect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer is also guilty` IF
        `the company committed an offence`
    AND (   (`the officer consented` AND `the officer connived`)
         OR `it is attributable to the officer's neglect`)

§§ `19, 20 -- defences`

-- s 19(1): a defence for the accused to prove (a) the offence was due to "a mistake ... or to reliance on information supplied ... or
-- to the act or default of another person, an accident or some other cause beyond" their control; AND (b) they "took all reasonable
-- precautions and exercised all due diligence".
-- s 19(2): if the defence blames another person or that person's information, it cannot be relied on "without permission of the
-- court" unless a written notice identifying that person was served on the prosecutor "within a period ending 7 clear days before
-- the hearing" (annotated Act 25 of 2021, wef 1 April 2022).
GIVEN `the cause was mistake, reliance, another's act, accident or beyond control` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `took all reasonable precautions and due diligence` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the defence blames another person` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `served notice at least 7 clear days before the hearing` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the court gave permission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the due diligence defence is available` IF
        `the cause was mistake, reliance, another's act, accident or beyond control`
    AND `took all reasonable precautions and due diligence`
    AND (    (NOT `the defence blames another person`)
         OR  `served notice at least 7 clear days before the hearing`
         OR  `the court gave permission`)

-- s 19(3): on a charge of SUPPLYING goods bearing a false trade description, a defence to prove the accused "did not know, and could
-- not with reasonable diligence have ascertained", that the goods did not conform or that the description had been applied.
GIVEN `charged with supplying` IS A BOOLEAN, `could not with reasonable diligence have known` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the innocent supplier defence is available` IF
    `charged with supplying` AND `could not with reasonable diligence have known`

-- s 20: for an offence committed by publishing an advertisement, a defence to prove (a) the accused's business is publishing
-- advertisements and (b) they received it "in the ordinary course of business and did not know and had no reason to suspect" that
-- publishing it would be an offence.
GIVEN `publishing advertisements is the business` IS A BOOLEAN, `received in the ordinary course of business` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `had no reason to suspect an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the innocent publisher defence is available` IF
        `publishing advertisements is the business`
    AND `received in the ordinary course of business`
    AND `had no reason to suspect an offence`

§§ `26(3) -- seized goods with no prosecution`

-- s 26(3): with no prosecution, seized goods "are deemed to be forfeited at the end of one month from the date of the seizure unless a
-- claim to the goods seized is made before then" by written notice to the Director (s 26(4)). Time is in months.
GIVEN `a prosecution was brought` IS A BOOLEAN, `months since seizure` IS A NUMBER, `the owner claimed in writing in time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the goods are deemed forfeited` IF
        (NOT `a prosecution was brought`)
    AND `months since seizure` AT LEAST 1
    AND (NOT `the owner claimed in writing in time`)

§§ `31 -- compensation orders`

-- s 31(1): on conviction the court may order compensation "not exceeding $1,000" for loss or damage resulting from the offence.
-- s 31(2): the order "does not affect any right to a civil action for the recovery of damages beyond the amount of compensation paid".
-- s 29 (not modelled): a contract "is not void or unenforceable by reason only of a contravention" of the Act.
GIVEN `the loss` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most the court may order as compensation` MEANS
    IF `the loss` GREATER THAN 1000 THEN 1000 ELSE `the loss`

GIVEN `the loss` IS A NUMBER, `the compensation paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the damages left to claim in a civil action` MEANS
    `the loss` MINUS `the compensation paid`
